WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.220
In 2018, the United States put new tariffs
on imported large washing machines.

2
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.700
A tariff is a tax on imports.

3
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.940
The government collects the revenue.

4
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.870
But where does that
money really come from?

5
00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:16.460
Economists tracked what happened next:

6
00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.860
to washers, to rival brands,

7
00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:22.040
and even to the dryers
sold right next to them.

8
00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.720
So when a country taxes goods from abroad,

9
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.920
who ends up paying, and
who comes out ahead?

10
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.710
In this mission, you'll
build the tariff graph step

11
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.350
by step and see where each
slice of surplus goes.

12
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.180
Then you'll set the tariff
yourself and predict what

13
00:00:37.180 --> 00:00:39.200
happens to government revenue.

14
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.840
Your mission: find out who
really pays for a tariff.
